1
00:00:01,200 --> 00:00:01,700
Ohhh!

2
00:00:01,780 --> 00:00:02,580
Meet oa and ow.

3
00:00:03,720 --> 00:00:06,340
Two spellings, one long O sound.

4
00:00:07,020 --> 00:00:08,320
You hear it in boat.

5
00:00:09,320 --> 00:00:10,680
And in snow.

6
00:00:11,980 --> 00:00:13,920
Same sound, different spelling.

7
00:00:14,440 --> 00:00:15,640
So which one do we write?

8
00:00:16,760 --> 00:00:18,060
Ask the same question.

9
00:00:18,940 --> 00:00:20,180
WHERE is the sound?

10
00:00:21,020 --> 00:00:24,540
At the beginning, in the middle, or at the end?

11
00:00:25,860 --> 00:00:28,020
In the MIDDLE, we write oa.

12
00:00:29,200 --> 00:00:29,440
B.

13
00:00:29,980 --> 00:00:29,980
Oa.

14
00:00:30,880 --> 00:00:31,680
T.

15
00:00:31,800 --> 00:00:32,460
Boat!

16
00:00:33,180 --> 00:00:34,860
Letters on both sides of it.

17
00:00:35,940 --> 00:00:37,940
At the END, we write ow.

18
00:00:39,340 --> 00:00:39,780
Sn.

19
00:00:40,180 --> 00:00:40,800
Ow.

20
00:00:41,780 --> 00:00:42,380
Snow!

21
00:00:42,860 --> 00:00:43,900
Nothing after it.

22
00:00:44,540 --> 00:00:46,080
So we use ow.

23
00:00:46,880 --> 00:00:48,780
We never write bowt.

24
00:00:49,700 --> 00:00:51,460
And we never write snoa.

25
00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:54,000
Oa in the middle.

26
00:00:54,680 --> 00:00:55,800
Ow at the end.

27
00:00:56,400 --> 00:00:57,080
Let's see it.

28
00:00:58,200 --> 00:00:58,520
Boat.

29
00:01:01,320 --> 00:01:01,780
Coat.

30
00:01:03,300 --> 00:01:03,740
Goat.

31
00:01:03,740 --> 00:01:04,820
Road.

32
00:01:04,880 --> 00:01:05,320
Toast.

33
00:01:06,900 --> 00:01:07,140
Soap.

34
00:01:08,500 --> 00:01:10,520
All oa, all in the middle.

35
00:01:11,560 --> 00:01:12,200
Now the end.

36
00:01:13,660 --> 00:01:14,120
Snow.

37
00:01:15,200 --> 00:01:15,840
Grow.

38
00:01:17,140 --> 00:01:17,660
Blow.

39
00:01:18,800 --> 00:01:19,640
Slow.

40
00:01:20,860 --> 00:01:21,620
Show.

41
00:01:23,060 --> 00:01:23,580
Yellow.

42
00:01:24,660 --> 00:01:26,840
All ow, all at the end.

43
00:01:27,760 --> 00:01:28,480
Your turn!

44
00:01:28,900 --> 00:01:31,480
Here's the word.

45
00:01:31,480 --> 00:01:31,980
Road.

46
00:01:32,860 --> 00:01:34,740
Is it oa, or ow?

47
00:01:36,720 --> 00:01:37,820
It's oa!

48
00:01:38,260 --> 00:01:39,680
The sound is in the middle.

49
00:01:40,280 --> 00:01:41,140
So remember.

50
00:01:41,640 --> 00:01:45,320
Oa sails in the middle, ow rolls to the end.

51
00:01:46,640 --> 00:01:49,640
Read more words like these in the English Learning app.

52
00:01:50,400 --> 00:01:51,690
Free to download today!
